      to the people playing them;
    </li>
    <li>
      the security of your RCON credentials. They are stored unencrypted on your machine so the App
      can use them, and Source RCON sends them over the network unencrypted, which is a property of
      the protocol rather than of the App.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The App does not review, filter or validate commands before sending them, and it cannot tell
    you whether a command is safe to run on your server.
  </p>

